    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\ncoverage.py excludes a whole block when the line that opens it matches an exclusion\npattern. The `Cython.Coverage` plugin only excludes the matching line itself, so the\nblock's body still counts as missed. A common case is an `if TYPE_CHECKING:` guard\naround imports.\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\n`mod.pyx`:\n```cython\n# cython: linetrace=True\nimport typing as _t\n\nif _t.TYPE_CHECKING:\n    import os\n\ndef f():\n    return 42\n```\n\n`pymod.py`: the same code, with the directive line replaced by a plain comment.\n\n`main.py`:\n```python\nimport mod, pymod\n\nmod.f()\npymod.f()\n```\n\n`.coveragerc`:\n```ini\n[run]\nplugins = Cython.Coverage\n\n[report]\nexclude_also =\n    ^\\s*if _t\\.TYPE_CHECKING:\n```\n\n```console\n$ CPPFLAGS=\"-DCYTHON_TRACE=1 -DCYTHON_USE_SYS_MONITORING=0\" cythonize -i mod.pyx\n$ coverage run main.py\n$ coverage report -m\nName       Stmts   Miss  Cover   Missing\n----------------------------------------\nmain.py        3      0   100%\nmod.pyx        5      1    80%   5\npymod.py       3      0   100%\n----------------------------------------\nTOTAL         11      1    91%\n```\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\n`import os` (line 5) is excluded in `mod.pyx`, as it is in `pymod.py`. From\ncoverage's docs: \"If a matched line introduces a block, the entire block is excluded\nfrom reporting.\"\n\n### OS\n\nLinux\n\n### Python version\n\n3.13.2\n\n### Cython version\n\n3.3.0; also master @ a76568d4e9cce24843e5b9e41f67e4dd5d8a6773\n\n### Additional context\n\n`_parse_cfile_lines()` matches each line separately, so block exclusion (and\nmulti-line exclusion regexes) can't work for `.pyx` files. Per-line exclusion was\nadded in #3680 / #3682, and #1820 proposed block-aware exclusion but stalled.\n\nCoverage.py 7.16.2.\n\nSeen in ansible/pylibssh#885.\n",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
